Carafe: the in-process server keeps device files, as the kernel does on Windows: a name the HID driver of the
overlay knows opens a device object, ioctls on it go to that driver, ReadFile takes its next input report or
waits for one as an overlapped operation that a new report completes, WriteFile goes to the driver too, and a
device object is signalled when its I/O ends, so a synchronous ReadFile waits on it as on a file.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

